<v Kristen>I used to always-- I don't even know if I should say this --I used to like to talk about fantasies of kidnapping him, and torturing him, and forcing him to transfer money into my bank account. But you know, I would just always joke about the things I would do to that man that would just make him feel uncomfortable and terrified. That's what I wanted to do more than anything.
<v Kristen>我以前总是——我甚至不知道我该不该说这个——我以前喜欢谈论那些绑架他、折磨他、强迫他把钱转到我银行账户的幻想。但你知道的，我总是拿我对那个男人做的事开玩笑，那些会让他感到不舒服和惊恐的事。比起什么都想做，我最想做的就是这个。

01:02:18.500 --> 01:02:42.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kristen's revenge fantasy is very similar to the plot of the movie 9 to 5, which Kristen has never seen, because it came out in 1980, before she was born. All of which is to say this is an old story.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>克里斯汀的复仇幻想与电影《朝九晚五》的剧情非常相似，而克里斯汀从未看过这部电影，因为它在1980年上映，比她出生还要早。所有这些都说明，这是一个老套的故事。

01:02:42.030 --> 01:02:53.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kristen's anger bled. It bed into her thoughts, her work. She remembers being at a conference and interviewing an older man, a guy in his 70s, about drug policy.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>克里斯汀的愤怒在蔓延。它渗透进她的思绪，她的工作。她记得自己曾在一个会议上采访过一个老头，一个70多岁关于毒品政策的家伙。

01:02:53.020 --> 01:03:11.700
<v Kristen>And at the end, I said I was going to smoke a cigarette, and he said, you don't want to get cancer in those boobs, do you? And I was just like, ew, and just got up and went outside and smoked a cigarette, and told all the people at the conference, can you believe that this dinosaur man just said that to me?
<v Kristen>最后，我说我要去抽根烟，他说，你可不想让那些胸部长癌吧？我当时就想，真恶心，然后起身走到外面抽烟，并把会议上的所有人都告诉了，你们能相信刚才那个老恐龙竟然对我说那种话吗？

01:03:11.700 --> 01:03:27.620
<v Kristen>And it was the same thing I felt with Don, like it was this older man who was just kind of like, I'm going to force the fact that I have a sexuality on you. I'm going to force you to reckon with it by making you the object of my sexual desire.
<v Kristen>这和我跟唐在一起时的感觉一模一样，就像这个老男人一副“我要把我的性欲强加给你”的架势。我要通过把你的变成我性欲的对象，来逼你面对这件事。

01:03:27.620 --> 01:03:37.190
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Later that day, Kristen was walking with her AlterNet colleague, Jan Frel. Not Don, Jan. Jan was, at various points, Don's second-in-command.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那天晚些时候，克里斯汀和她的AlterNet同事简·弗雷尔（Jan Frel）一起散步。不是唐，是简。简在不同时期一直是唐的副手。

01:03:37.190 --> 01:04:12.400
<v Kristen>And we were walking down the sidewalk, and he was on the left of me, and traffic was on the other side of him, and I told him what happened, and he said, oh, well, you must have taken it as a compliment, kind of, though, right? Or something like that. And I just had this image of pushing him into the street that was so vivid, it almost freaked me out. I was like, I came very close to maybe killing this person. But that's how full of rage I was by that point. I was just about to explode.
<v Kristen>我们走在人行道上，他在我的左边，车流在他的另一侧，我把发生的事告诉了他，他说，哦，好吧，你多少还是把它当成了一种赞美，对吧？或者类似这样的话。我脑海里顿时浮现出把他推向马路的画面，那个画面是如此清晰，甚至把我吓坏了。我想，我差一点点就把这个人给杀了。但当时的我就是充满了如此多的怒火。我当时简直快要爆炸了。

01:04:12.400 --> 01:04:42.810
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Jan does remember Kristen telling him about this, but does not recall responding in this way. Kristen started talking. She told a female coworker named Lauren about how Don was treating her. Lauren was a bit older, seemed together, but she didn't know what to do. She did have one idea of someone who could help, a woman Lauren actually had just met at a book party, a woman in her 30s who had worked with Don in the past. Her name was Deanna.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>简确实记得克里斯汀跟他说过这事，但不记得自己曾这样回应过。克里斯汀开始四处倾诉。她把唐是如何对待她的事告诉了一位名叫劳伦的女同事。劳伦稍微年长一些，看起来很稳重，但她也不知道该怎么办。她确实想到了一个可以帮忙的人，一个劳伦其实刚刚在图书派对上认识的女人，一个30多岁、过去曾在唐手下工作过的女人。她的名字叫迪娜。

01:04:42.810 --> 01:04:46.530
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Lauren asked to talk to Deanna, Deanna remembers.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>劳伦要求和迪娜谈谈，迪娜回忆说。

01:04:46.530 --> 01:04:53.490
<v Deanna>She started telling me about the experiences this new staffer was having with him, this young woman.
<v Deanna>她开始跟我讲述这个新员工在他手下经历的事情，这个年轻的女性。

01:04:53.490 --> 01:05:08.370
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Deanna hadn't been with Don for years at this point. Lauren didn't know they'd ever been together. But Lauren told Deanna, part of what's so hard about this is the new staffer is so young and inexperienced. Don met her when she was a student on the street at a protest.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>此时的迪娜已经离开唐好多年了。劳伦并不知道她们俩曾经在一起过。但劳伦对迪娜说，这其中最难熬的部分在于，这个新员工太年轻、太没有经验了。唐是在街头的一场抗议活动中遇到她的，当时她还是个学生。

01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:26.000
<v Deanna>And I was like, you've got to be fucking kidding me. I was fucking there. I should have taken her by the wrist, pulled her away with me, and said, do not. I will find you another job, you know. And I felt such guilt over that.
<v Deanna>我当时想，你他妈在逗我吧。我他妈当时就在现场。我当时本该抓住她的手腕，把她从那儿拉开，对她说，千万别去。我知道你可以找另一份工作，你知道的。我为此感到极大的负罪感。

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:38.170
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Deanna began cycling through the moments, all the choices she had made, that she thought were just hers, choices she assumed would only affect her and her relationship with Don.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>迪娜开始在脑海中反复回放那些时刻，她做过的所有选择，她曾以为这些选择只属于她自己，她曾以为这些选择只会影响她自己以及她和唐的关系。

01:05:38.170 --> 01:06:09.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She thought specifically about a call she got years ago, just two months after she'd broken up with Don. It was a professional contact who said she wanted to ask Deanna about something serious. And then the woman on the phone said that her organization had put on an event with AlterNet, and a young staffer had just complained that Don sexually harassed her. The woman on the phone said to Deanna, you've worked with Don. Does that sound like him? Deanna paused to consider it before answering.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她特别想到了多年前接到的一通电话，就在她和唐分手仅仅两个月后。那是她的一位职业人脉，说她想跟迪娜谈谈一件严肃的事。然后电话那头的女人说，她们的机构曾与AlterNet共同举办过一场活动，一名年轻员工刚刚投诉说唐对她进行了性骚扰。电话里的女人对迪娜说，你和唐共事过。这听起来像他会做的事吗？迪娜在回答前停顿了一下，仔细考虑了一番。

01:06:09.650 --> 01:06:25.350
<v Deanna>I have a lot of shame, but my greatest shame was-- I can't picture him doing something unwanted, was what I said. And so I kind of-- I defended him. I didn't kind of defend him. Like, I didn't say, I believe this person.
<v Deanna>我有很多羞耻感，但我最大的羞耻感是——我说的是，我无法想象他会做出那种不请自来的事。所以我算是——我为他进行了辩护。我可不仅仅是为他辩护。就像，我没有说，我相信这个人。

01:06:25.350 --> 01:06:29.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But was true for you at the time that you couldn't imagine him doing that?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但当时对你来说，你真的无法想象他会做那种事吗？

01:06:29.770 --> 01:06:47.360
<v Deanna>(DRAGGING THE WORD OUT INTO A GROAN) No. Yeah, but I-- there was a tiny part of me that wondered if that could be true, and I just didn't want to deal with it, and nothing was ever done. It never went further.
<v Deanna>（把声音拖成一声长长的哀叹）不。是的，但是，我——我内心有一个微小的声音在纳闷这会不会是真的，而我只是不想去面对它，而且什么也没做。这件事再也没有往下发展。

01:06:47.360 --> 01:07:00.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Deanna and Kristen went out for drinks. Deanna listened, Kristen talked. Deanna said she wanted to help in whatever way she could, and Deanna prayed that Kristen would not ask her, what happened to you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>迪娜和克里斯汀一起出去喝了酒。迪娜听着，克里斯汀倾诉着。迪娜说她愿意提供任何力所能及的帮助，而迪娜在心里祈祷克里斯汀千万不要问她：你身上发生过什么？

01:07:00.150 --> 01:07:32.190
<v Deanna>Everything felt like it would blow up. Everyone would know that I was complicit, that I helped him. How could people want to be friends with me after that? How could people trust my professional expertise after knowing that about me? How could-- what would my mom think? They're all going to think I'm a fraud, that I'm not talented, that I'm not-- that these ideas aren't my own or something, and I would just have to shrink away.
<v Deanna>一切感觉都快要崩塌了。所有人都会知道我是同谋，是我帮了他。在那之后，人们怎么还会想跟我做朋友？在得知了我这些事之后，人们怎么还能信任我的专业技能？怎么会——我妈会怎么想？他们都会觉得我是一个骗子，觉得我根本没有才华，觉得——这些想法根本不是我自己的或者别的什么，而我只能退缩逃避。

01:07:32.190 --> 01:08:02.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Deanna helped connect Kristen with a lawyer. The lawyer told Kristin it would be very hard to win a lawsuit and keep her job. She also said she'd probably need more evidence. And that's when Kristen thought to ask Tana. She knew Don had been harassing her, too. Kristen doesn't remember Tana saying, this isn't news that this happens. She remembers Tana being kind, and saying she didn't want to betray Don. He'd given her a chance and a career when no one else would have.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>迪娜帮克里斯汀联系了一位律师。律师告诉克里斯汀，要想赢得官司并保住工作将非常困难。她还说她可能需要更多证据。就在那时，克里斯汀想到了去问塔娜。她知道唐也曾骚扰过塔娜。克里斯汀不记得塔娜说过“这发生又不是什么新闻”。她只记得塔娜很友善，说她不想背叛唐。当别人都不肯给机会时，是唐给了她机会和职业生涯。

01:08:02.970 --> 01:08:07.750
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So she said she didn't want to do it, and then what did you do?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以她说她不想这么做，然后你做了什么？

01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:15.630
<v Kristen>I just kind of gave up.
<v Kristen>我差不多就放弃了。

01:08:15.630 --> 01:08:26.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kristen's apartment flooded, and she got a payout from her landlord. When the money came in, she quit AlterNet without ever using the words she believed to be true.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>克里斯汀的公寓被水淹了，她从房东那里拿到了赔偿金。当这笔钱到账时，她从AlterNet辞职了，自始至终没有说出那些她坚信为真的词。

01:08:26.820 --> 01:08:59.480
<v Kristen>When I left, I didn't say to him, I'm leaving because you sexually harassed me, and I hate you. I was too affected by the idea that he was giving you a chance. And it's true, he did give us a chance that no one else did. So I mean-- but I guess I felt like I had paid my dues, and the payoff was no longer fair.
<v Kristen>当我离开时，我没有对他说，我离开是因为你性骚扰了我，我恨你。我被“他曾给你一个机会”这种想法深深地影响了。而且这是真的，他确实给了我们一个别人不曾给过的机会。所以我的意思是——但我想我当时觉得我已经付出了代价，而回报已经不再公平了。

01:08:59.480 --> 01:09:03.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Act 7, "Vivian."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>第七幕，“薇薇安”。

01:09:03.060 --> 01:09:24.920
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Four years after Tana told Kristen that their experience was not news to anyone, suddenly it was news. A reporter named Cora Lewis at BuzzFeed News reported a story about sexual harassment allegations at AlterNet. She talked to Kristen and Tana and Deanna, and she talked to other women who haven't heard from here.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在塔娜告诉克里斯汀她们的经历对任何人来说都不是新闻的四年后，它突然成了新闻。BuzzFeed新闻的一位名叫科拉·刘易斯（Cora Lewis）的记者报道了一则关于AlterNet性骚扰指控的故事。她采访了克里斯汀、塔娜和迪娜，还采访了其他我们在这里没有听到其声音的女性。

01:09:24.920 --> 01:10:02.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Don denied most of the allegations in the BuzzFeed story. Some he said were mischaracterized. For instance, he does not remember twisting Tana's arm, but did say he was rubbing her shoulders and stopped when he saw it made her uncomfortable. He does not remember showing Tana a photograph of his penis, but says he does have such a photograph, and some women may have seen it. He said he also took friendly photos in the office, and when he commented on Tana's body, it was out of concern that she was getting too skinny. The photo he showed Kristen, he said, was not a naked porn star, but a clothed movie star.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>唐否认了BuzzFeed报道中的大部分指控。他说有些指控被失实地描述了。例如，他不记得自己曾扭转塔娜的胳膊，但确实说过他曾揉过她的肩膀，并在发现这让她感到不舒服时停了下来。他不记得自己曾给塔娜看过一张自己阴茎的照片，但他说他确实有这样一张照片，有些女性可能看过。他说他还曾在办公室里拍过友好的照片，当他对塔娜的身材发表评论时，是出于担心她变得太瘦。他说，他给克里斯汀看的照片不是一个赤裸的色情明星，而是一个穿著衣服的电影明星。

01:10:02.400 --> 01:10:42.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When I contacted Don, he said he told Deanna about his relationship with Vivian, his partner, on their very first date, and that his memory of their time at Big Sur is different from hers. Beyond that, he did not respond to specific questions, but asked that I include an apology from him, in which he says, along the way, I strove but apparently failed to treat everyone with the respect and consideration they deserved. I regret causing harm, and I'm reckoning with it. Some of the accusations against me are untrue, but I deeply regret those that are. I apologize to anyone I offended and treated badly.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当我联系唐时，他说他在第一次约会时就将自己与伴侣薇薇安的关系告诉了迪娜，并且他对在大苏尔那段时光的记忆与迪娜的不同。除此之外，他没有回答具体的问题，而是请求我加入一段他的道歉，其中他写道：一路上，我努力但显然未能以应有的尊重和关怀对待每个人。我为造成的伤害感到后悔，我正在对此进行反思。对我的一些指控是不真实的，但我对那些属实的指控深感遗憾。我向任何被我冒犯和恶劣对待过的人道歉。

01:10:42.030 --> 01:11:07.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Before the BuzzFeed News story came out, Vivian says Don told her he needed to talk to her about something, to prepare her. Vivian told me she knew what it was, Me Too stories coming for Don. She'd pictured how their conversation would go. When Don sat her down, it was not what she'd imagined. He told her, 10 years ago he'd had an affair with Deanna.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在BuzzFeed新闻报道出来之前，薇薇安说唐告诉她，他有件事需要跟她谈谈，好让她有个心理准备。薇薇安告诉我，她知道那是什么，那是冲着唐来的“我也是”故事。她已经在脑海中想象过他们的对话会如何展开。当唐让她坐下时，情况却和她想象的完全不一样。他告诉她，10年他和迪娜有过一段外遇。

01:11:07.400 --> 01:11:07.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦——

01:11:07.970 --> 01:11:08.540
<v Vivian>And--
<v Vivian>然后——

01:11:08.540 --> 01:11:08.920
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>--you didn't--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>——你没有——

01:11:08.920 --> 01:11:09.690
<v Vivian>Yeah.
<v Vivian>是的。

01:11:09.690 --> 01:11:12.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You didn't-- he hadn't told you about it before.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你没有——他以前没有跟你说过这事。

01:11:12.470 --> 01:11:18.140
<v Vivian>He hadn't told-- no, this is all-- I am assimilating all of this in the past month.
<v Vivian>他没有说过——没有，这一切——我是在过去的一个月里才把所有这些消化完的。

01:11:18.140 --> 01:11:19.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Wow.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哇。

01:11:19.630 --> 01:11:26.460
<v Vivian>Yeah. I went crazy. I mean, I just sort of screamed, you have no idea what you've done.
<v Vivian>是的。我简直要疯了。我的意思是，我只是大喊大叫，你根本不知道你干了什么。

01:11:26.460 --> 01:11:27.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Immediately, you did?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你立刻就这么做了？

01:11:27.890 --> 01:11:30.020
<v Vivian>Oh God, yes.
<v Vivian>哦天哪，是的。

01:11:30.020 --> 01:11:46.910
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She wanted to understand why he did this. She tried to remember what was happening in his life around that time, and there was a lot. Moving his elderly parents, trying to take responsibility for a sister who was ill and suffering a psychotic break, his own health issues.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她想弄明白他为什么要这么做。她试图回想当时他的生活里发生了什么，事情确实很多。搬迁年迈的父母，试图为一个患病且正在经受精神崩溃的姐姐承担责任，他自己的健康问题。

01:11:46.910 --> 01:11:55.340
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Vivian is a therapist, and from Don, Vivian solicited details, assembled details, as a therapist does.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>薇薇安是一名治疗师，从唐那里，薇薇安索取细节，拼凑细节，就像一个治疗师所做的那样。

01:11:55.340 --> 01:12:08.730
<v Vivian>For myself. I mean, this was not playing therapist for him. This was just like, I have got to make sense of this somehow. I've got to. I'm still working on that. Don't get me wrong. He's got to, too.
<v Vivian>为了我自己。我的意思是，这不是在为他扮演治疗师。这纯粹就像，我必须以某种方式把这一切弄明白。我必须这么做。我还在为此努力。别误会。他也必须这么做。

01:12:08.730 --> 01:12:10.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why do you have to make sense of it?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你为什么必须把它弄明白？

01:12:10.600 --> 01:12:23.350
<v Vivian>It's what I do. Its who I am. It feels like the only way to be a person with a history that feels coherent.
<v Vivian>这就是我的工作。这就是我是谁。这感觉像是拥有一个连贯历史的人的唯一活法。

01:12:23.350 --> 01:12:28.790
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>A person with a history that feels coherent with him? Like, your history with him?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>一个与他有着连贯历史的人？比如，你和他的历史？

01:12:28.790 --> 01:12:33.940
<v Vivian>Yes, absolutely. It's so hard to integrate.
<v Vivian>是的，绝对的。这太难去整合了。

01:12:33.940 --> 01:12:37.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Are you going to stay with him?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你还要和他在一起吗？

01:12:37.440 --> 01:12:43.780
<v Vivian>I'm 99.9 certain we will make it through this.
<v Vivian>我有99.9%的把握我们能挺过这一关。

01:12:43.780 --> 01:13:16.910
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Don had just destroyed the story Vivian had about their relationship, a coherent history that for Vivian had included a wonderful partner with whom she shared a joyful life, shared trips and friends and intellectual interests, a partner who took loving care of her last year when Vivian was in chemotherapy for breast cancer. To stay with him and to make her history coherent, Vivian is trying to figure out what she needs to know, and how to resist asking about the things she does not need to know.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>唐刚刚摧毁了薇薇安关于他们关系的叙事——一段对薇薇安来说包含着美妙伴侣的连贯历史，他们曾共享快乐的生活、共同的旅行、朋友和智识兴趣，一个去年在薇薇安因乳腺癌接受化疗时给予她充满爱意的照顾的伴侣。为了和他在一起并让她的历史保持连贯，薇薇安正在努力弄清楚她需要知道什么，以及如何克制自己不去打听那些她不需要知道的事情。

01:13:16.910 --> 01:13:37.720
<v Vivian>I want to know about stupid things like, did they share the music that we love? You know, things like that, things that have always felt very special and intimate. I want to know what was shared that's always felt exclusive.
<v Vivian>我想知道那些愚蠢的事情，比如，他们分享过我们热爱的音乐吗？你知道的，诸如此类的事情，那些一直让人觉得非常特别和私密的事情。我想知道有哪些曾经觉得是独一无二的东西被分享了出去。

01:13:37.720 --> 01:13:59.100
<v Vivian>We were watching a movie the other night, and one character was holding another in a certain way. And I just broke down, and just said, did you hold her that way? He said, no, when I saw that, I just thought, that's you and me. And I believe him.
<v Vivian>前几天晚上我们在看一部电影，其中一个角色以某种方式抱着另一个角色。我当时彻底崩溃了，直接问：你这样抱过她吗？他说，没有，我看到那个时，我只是想，那是你和我。我相信他。

01:13:59.100 --> 01:14:42.830
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Four days before Christmas, Don's story was added to the news of allegations about sexual harassment and violence that suddenly have a public platform in this stunning period of time that is right now. Don's story came after the one about Harvey Weinstein, and Mario Batali, and Louis CK, and Senator Al Franken, Matt Lauer, and Charlie Rose, and Russell Simmons, and Dustin Hoffman, and Kevin Spacey, editors at the New Republic, DC Comics, the Paris Review, the head of NPR News, the owner of an NFL team, and the choreographer of a ballet. After Don's story came Congressman Patrick Meehan, Michael Douglas, Rob Porter and the sentencing of Larry Nassar.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在圣诞节前四天，唐的故事被添加到了那些关于性骚扰和性暴力的指控新闻中，这些指控在这个令人震惊的时代突然登上了公共平台。唐的故事继哈维·韦恩斯坦、马里奥·巴塔利、路易·C·K、参议员阿尔·弗兰肯、马特·劳尔、查理·罗斯、拉塞尔·西蒙斯、达斯汀·霍夫曼、凯文·空间、《新共和》杂志的编辑、DC漫画、《巴黎评论》、NPR新闻负责人、NFL球队老板以及芭蕾舞编导的故事之后浮出水面。在唐的故事之后，还有众议员帕特里克·米汉、迈克尔·道格拉斯、罗布·波特以及对拉里·纳萨尔的判决。

01:14:42.830 --> 01:15:02.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The board that oversees AlterNet said they were investigating the allegations in detail. That investigation did not include reaching out to any of the women named in this story or in the BuzzFeed article. I don't know how you can understand what happened without speaking to the people who are saying, something happened to me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>监督AlterNet的董事会表示，他们正在详细调查这些指控。该调查并不包括联系本故事或BuzzFeed文章中提及的任何女性。我不知道在不与那些说“有什么事情发生在我身上了”的人对话的情况下，你究竟怎么能理解发生了什么。

